is_anomaly: true
faulty_devices: srv1
diagnosis_text:
- Affected component: The HTTP web service (Apache) on the internal server srv1 (10.5.0.4).
- Mechanism: Office PCs resolve internal names correctly, but the web daemon on srv1 is not listening on TCP/80 (or 443). As a result, browsers receive a connection refusal and render “site can’t be found/can’t be reached,” which is often misinterpreted as a DNS issue.
- Localization: Host srv1, interface eth0 (10.5.0.4). On clients (e.g., pc1), DNS is set to use 10.5.0.4 and resolves srv1.jeremysitlab.com to 10.5.0.4 (nslookup succeeds; ping resolves and reaches 10.5.0.4). However, HTTP requests fail: from pc1, curl http://srv1.jeremysitlab.com and curl http://10.5.0.4 return “Connection refused.” On srv1, no sockets are listen
[FINAL] stop=no-more-tool-calls tool_calls=22
